ok: the UpgradeCap from the localnet publish is seeded on the fork
ok: the localnet package upgraded on the fork
ok: the upgrade produced a new package id
ok: the upgrade used the UpgradeCap from the localnet publish
ok: the upgraded package is at version 2 on the fork
ok: the new module is callable on the fork
=== counter/Published.toml after the fork upgrade ===
[published.fork]
version = 2
[published.localnet]
version = 1
=== the localnet is untouched ===
ok: the original package is still readable on the localnet
ok: the upgraded package does not exist on the localnet
ok: the localnet's UpgradeCap is one version behind the fork's

